Aftermath:  11 minutes after contact was lost the rescue team arrived at the scene to find most of the capture team killed in various gruesome ways. Whilst most of the agents had been burned beyond recognition there were some who had been impaled on large structures of ice and strung up in an almost ritualistic manner. Those not burned had been impaled and strung up in a circle with their limbs outstretched in various ways by the ice as if praying. The remains of the bullets fired at the entity were later recovered having seemingly frozen and shattered on impact.

Only one survivor was found with his body covered in second- and third-degree burns covering roughly 63 percent of his body. Agent Alex Moore spent several months in recovery and underwent several surgeries before being able to fully describe what had happened. He later confirmed that SCP-XXXX did indeed possess thermokinetic abilities and used them to kill the other agents, he also described how the entity propped him up against a tree and made him watch as it strung up the other agents after having burned him, having seemingly deliberately avoided killing him.

Agent A. Moore's description of events seem to suggest that SCP-5129 kills for some ritualistic purpose and or that it takes some sort of sick pleasure in killing.

Until further notice no other attempts to capture SCP-5129 are to be authorized. Additionally further research is to be focused on the entity’s abilities and reasoning.
